{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"petalous-spicey-cirriped","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Defect\n\nAfter a ticket-store fast-forward sync, `rebar review-plan religious-freakish-muskox` returned the same stale BLOCK findings from an earlier review instead of evaluating the current amended description. The current ticket description contains the reviewer-requested heartbeat-lane test inventory, but the latest audit record still pins the old material.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Current `religious-freakish-muskox` description length: 7181.\n- Latest audit plan-review `reviewed_at`: 1788763607491207001.\n- Latest audit plan-review `verified_at_sha`: 7a0ecc400c32de3bf09b887c1d8bc44f960358d3.\n- Latest audit material description part: ['1b886c746f4807f7', 3539].\n- The stale blocking findings still say the plan names only the 24f7 test, even though current description lines enumerate `test_heartbeat_alert_closes_on_recovery` and `test_close_argv_exact_shape`.\n- `git -C .tickets-tracker pull --ff-only origin tickets` reported `Already up to date` before the rerun.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A review-plan invocation after a ticket description edit evaluates the current ticket material or refuses with an explicit stale-material error.\n- [ ] The audit/status output makes it possible to distinguish a reused old result from a newly evaluated review.\n- [ ] A regression test covers a description edit followed by review-plan so stale findings cannot be reported as if they evaluated the new material.\n","id":"5319-1263-e7bc-4f17","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"review-plan reuses stale material after description edit"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788783765064470001,"uuid":"51d4114c-b454-4aea-acee-ab3e1ceeebc2"}